WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.618
Week 31: Comparison, Register, and Idiomatic Force. make a nuanced comparison praise or criticize appropriately interpret idioms from context

2
00:00:10.618 --> 00:00:25.399
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can make a nuanced comparison, praise or criticize appropriately, interpret idioms from context. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:25.399 --> 00:00:34.310
Language system. Advanced comparisons; superlatives; adverb placement; intensifiers; selected idioms and pragmatic limits.

4
00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:41.600
Sound and delivery. Discourse stress, intensification, and avoiding a flat word-by-word delivery.

5
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:51.133
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:51.133 --> 00:01:23.599
Model language. La segunda opción es mucho más viable. — The second option is much more viable. El informe menos claro fue el primero. — The least clear report was the first one. El proyecto va viento en popa. — The project is going very well. Ese dato hay que tomarlo con pinzas. — That data point should be treated cautiously. Su análisis dio en el clavo; sin embargo, faltan pruebas. — His or her analysis hit the nail on the head; however, evidence is still lacking.

7
00:01:23.599 --> 00:01:33.753
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
